course: dictionary
lesson: 15522
title: Proving it: substantiating
level: primary-6
stars: 3
explain: Substantiating is a long, formal word. It means proving that something is true by giving facts or evidence. «The scientist ran the test again to substantiate her claim.» She did not just say her idea was right. She showed results that backed it up.
explain: As an adjective, substantiating describes the facts or evidence that do the proving. «Mia brought a ticket and a photo as substantiating evidence for her story.» The ticket and the photo are the proof that her story is true.
explain: You will meet this word in exams, law and science. In everyday talk, people say proving, backing up or supporting. When you see substantiating, try swapping in "proving" and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Substantiate is a verb. Its forms are substantiate, substantiates, substantiated and substantiating.
fact: «Substantiating» means proving that something is true with facts or evidence.
fact: As an adjective, «substantiating evidence» means evidence that supports a claim.
fact: A claim is a statement that someone says is true, such as «The bridge is safe».
fact: Substantiating is a formal word, so you will mostly see it in writing, exams and law.
exercise: «Mia showed a receipt as substantiating evidence for her story.» What job does the receipt do? | Invents a new story | Makes the story longer | Hides the facts | *Proves her story is true
exercise: Ella says substantiating means being very tired. What does it really mean? | *Showing facts or evidence that something is true | Being very tired | Hiding a secret | Singing a song
exercise: «The scientist repeated the test to substantiate her claim.» Find and copy the word that means the same as prove. | scientist | *substantiate | repeated | claim
test: «Without substantiating evidence, the judge could not believe the witness.» What does substantiating evidence mean here? | Evidence that is funny | Evidence that is kept secret | *Evidence that proves the claim is true | A long list of names
test: Which everyday word could replace substantiating in «substantiating a claim»? | *Backing up | Dropping | Forgetting | Hiding
exam: In the sentence «Her substantiating facts were checked by three experts», what do the facts do? | Make the sentence longer | Hide the truth | Make a joke | *Show that her claim is true
